"""
# No-GC Async Mutex Facade

Re-exports the no-GC sync mutex backend, including the guard-pattern
`with_lock` API (preferred over manual lock()/unlock()).

## WARNING: sync-backed — lock() BLOCKS the OS thread

The compatibility `Mutex` below remains sync-backed: `lock()`/`with_lock()` block the
calling OS thread instead of suspending the async task, so a contended lock
stalls every green thread scheduled on that carrier thread. Acceptable for
short critical sections only. Hosted poll tasks can use
`AsyncMutex.hosted(capacity)` from `std.async.sync` (also exported below): its
bounded owner parks through HostScheduler, hands off FIFO, and unlinks/releases
resources on scheduler terminal cancellation. The legacy green closure executor
has no resumable poll frame, so the compatibility APIs retain this warning:

doc/08_tracking/bug/async_mutex_blocks_carrier_thread_no_suspend_2026-07-28.md
"""

export use std.nogc_sync_mut.concurrent.mutex.{Mutex, mutex_new, mutex_with_lock, mutex_lock, mutex_try_lock, mutex_unlock}

export use std.async.sync.{AsyncMutex, HostedAsyncMutex, AsyncMutexLease}
